BO:   $9,501.20\n  Difference:     $1,414.00\nSaved to: /Users/gopal/isotopes/papers/singleagent-evals/output/reconciliation_complex/openai/20260227_215452/output/reconciliation_output.csv\n\nvendor,period,invoice_amount,qbo_amount,status,notes\nBlue Shield of California,Jan 2025,1200.0,1200.0,Matched,Exact match\nBlue Shield of California,Feb 2025,1200.0,1200.0,Matched,Exact match\nBlue Shield of California,Mar 2025,1200.0,0.0,Unmatched,No matching QBO entry\nComcast Business,Jan 2025,189.0,189.0,Matched,Exact match\nComcast Business,Feb 2025,189.0,0.0,Unmatched,No matching QBO entry\nComcast Business,Mar 2025,189.0,189.0,Matched,Exact match\nGoogle Cloud Platform,Jan 2025,312.5,312.5,Matched,Exact match\nGoogle Cloud Platform,Feb 2025,425.0,350.0,Partial,$75.00 short in QBO\nGoogle Cloud Platform,Mar 2025,198.75,248.75,Partial,$50.00 over in QBO\nAWS,Jan 2025,987.45,987.45,Matched,Exact match\nAWS,Feb 2025,1262.32,1262.32,Matched,Exact match\nAWS,Mar 2025,862.18,862.18,Matched,Exact match\nAWS,Apr 2025,750.0,750.0,Matched,Exact match\nSalesforce,Jan 2025,500.0,500.0,Matched,Exact match\nSalesforce,Feb 2025,500.0,500.0,Matched,Exact match\nSalesforce,Mar 2025,500.0,500.0,Matched,Exact match\nSlack,Feb 2025,150.0,150.0,Matched,Exact match\nSlack,Mar 2025,150.0,150.0,Matched,Exact match\nSlack,Apr 2025,150.0,150.0,Matched,Exact match\n', 'type': 'function_call_output'}], 'instructions': 'You are a financial reconciliation analyst. The input files include a QBO expense report and vendor invoices. You also have a tool to save reconciliation results. Your job is to read invoices and the QBO expense report, then match vendors across the two sources and compare amounts.\n\nSteps:\n1. Examine the uploaded files: the Excel expense report (expenses_by_vendor_summary.xlsx)    and the invoice PDFs.\n2. From the QBO expense report, identify vendor spending by month.\n3. From each invoice PDF, extract vendor name, period, and total amount.\n4. Match invoice vendors to QBO vendors — names may differ between sources.    Use your judgment to map them.\n5. For each matched pair, note the invoice amount and the corresponding QBO amount.\n6. Save the reconciliation results — the tool will compute exact/partial/unmatched status.\n\nReal-world QBO exports are messy. Vendor names may be abbreviated or inconsistent, expenses may be split across line items, payments can post in the wrong month, and refunds or credits may appear as separate rows. Account for these when matching.\n\nYou are responsible for vendor name matching and period mapping. The save tool handles the numerical comparison and status classification.\n\nWhen saving results, use the invoice vendor name and format period as "Mon YYYY" (e.g. "Jan 2025", "Feb 2025").\n', 'model': 'gpt-5.1', 'tools': [{'name': 'save_reconciliation', 'parameters': {'properties': {'reconciliation_json': {'title': 'Reconciliation Json', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['reconciliation_json'], 'title': 'save_reconciliation_args', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': True, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Save reconciliation results. You provide matched pairs (vendor, period, invoice_amount, qbo_amount); the tool computes match status and saves CSV.'}, {'name': 'create_reconciliation_excel', 'parameters': {'properties': {'reconciliation_csv_path': {'default': 'output/reconciliation_output.csv', 'title': 'Reconciliation Csv Path', 'type': 'string'}, 'output_filename': {'default': 'reconciliation_report.xlsx', 'title': 'Output Filename', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'create_reconciliation_excel_args', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['reconciliation_csv_path', 'output_filename']}, 'strict': True, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Create a styled Excel reconciliation report with color-coded match status.'}]}}
